ps://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/2145#issuecomment-264438598","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/2145","id":264438598,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NDQzODU5OA==","user":{"login":"mice777","id":3145438,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDU0Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3145438?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777","html_url":"https://github.com/mice777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-12-02T11:55:59Z","updated_at":"2016-12-02T11:55:59Z","body":"Compliant or not, I used a tool that shifted times to match movie, and it shifted some times to negative range. It played OK on a video player and I didn't care about negative ones.\r\nIt could play too in exoplayer by tiny fix:\r\n```private static final Pattern SUBRIP_TIMESTAMP = Pattern.compile(\"(?:(-?\\\\d+):)?(\\\\d+):(\\\\d+),(\\\\d+)\"); ```\r\n(added \"-?\")","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/264438598/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"mice777","id":3145438,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDU0Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3145438?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777","html_url":"https://github.com/mice777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/264441663","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/2145#issuecomment-264441663","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/2145","id":264441663,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NDQ0MTY2Mw==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-12-02T12:15:35Z","updated_at":"2016-12-02T12:15:35Z","body":"It seems preferable for you to ask whoever writes the tool you're using to fix the bug (i.e. by clipping the output to t=0). Making non-compliant additions to other software as a means to work around the problem is not the best approach, and furthermore, it encourages the creation of more tools that generate non-compliant output.\r\n\r\nUnless you can find a reference that says negative timestamps are allowed, I think you should report the issue to whoever created the tool and get a fix on that side.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/264441663/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/264445224","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/2145#issuecomment-264445224","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/2145","id":264445224,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NDQ0NTIyNA==","user":{"login":"mice777","id":3145438,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDU0Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3145438?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777","html_url":"https://github.com/mice777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-12-02T12:37:31Z","updated_at":"2016-12-02T12:38:02Z","body":"I don't remember the tool. But many players handled it.\r\n\r\nYou could simply ignore negative timestamps instead of breaking entire parsing. You have already \"Skipping invalid index: \" in there which is also support for non-compliant files.\r\n\r\nAnother point of view: Subrip is probably not standardized at form of \"RFC\" or similar. You you should point to make the parser as permissive as possible. Btw, are negative timecodes really documented somewhere to be prohibited?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/264445224/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"mice777","id":3145438,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxNDU0Mzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3145438?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777","html_url":"https://github.com/mice777","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mice777/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/264458156","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/2145#issuecomment-264458156","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/2145","id":264458156,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI2NDQ1ODE1Ng==","user":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-12-02T13:51:52Z","updated_at":"2016-12-02T13:51:52Z","body":"I see what you mean now. You're right. To clarify:\r\n\r\n- Whilst we don't want to actively handle the case (i.e. treat it as valid), we don't want to flat out fail playback either. I was thinking this was covered by the \"Skipping invalid timing\" logic case, but I guess the failure actually occurs in `parseTimecode` and is not currently handled gracefully. We will update the code to handle this by skipping to be consistent with the other cases.\r\n- Re what's really allowed. Yes, I'm equally unsure of whether there exists a definitive spec. The closest to authoritative sources I could find were the [WebVTT timestamp definition](https://www.w3.org/TR/webvtt1/#webvtt-timestamp) (which I think was based derived from SubRip) and [Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SubRip). Both of which appear to not allow negative timecodes.\r\n- As a general point I disagree with the \"parsers should be as permissive as possible\" comment. Parsers being overly permissive encourages content production tools to be non-compliant, and you end up in a cycle where a large proportion of content is non-compliant and where it's no longer possible to implement a viable parser just by reading a specification and doing what it says.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/264458156/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"ojw28","id":7881572,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc4ODE1NzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7881572?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28","html_url":"https://github.com/ojw28","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/gists{